<http://data.silknow.org/object/f4ee4a21-42ae-3ff2-b96a-1cfdd79a3928/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Epitaphios, the Lamentation. Central panel: foreground, Jesus upon a sheet supported by a man at either end (Joseph of Arimathea and Nicodemus?) is placed upon a bier. The three Marys look on from the center flanked by a pair of angels and a man (John?). Background, the cross; God admidst radiant clouds, a shaft of gold bearing a bird travels from his mouth downward. All figures have pearl lined halloes; the cross outlined and the bird encircled with pearls. Metallic and silk yarns; faces and hands painted over silk yarns, on a silk ground shot with vertical metal strips. Border: Russian brocade, semi-naturalistic floral sprays and blossoms repeating in floss silk and metallic yarns on a metallic and silk yarn ground. Metallic yarn fringe with floral pendants made of metal and strips with spangles. Paint cracked, yarns worn."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/f4ee4a21-42ae-3ff2-b96a-1cfdd79a3928> .

